@startuml packages
' accTitle: Package boundaries and application composition
' accDescr: ModalAnyware composes narrow UI, native key and plugin-management modules. It embeds the plugin framework, its own project, and is a client of the Machine server, another project that embeds the same framework for its provider plugins and holds the Machine package as its core. Configuration depends only on public TypeScript APIs. The first-party plugin is a bundled plugin package that reaches resident app facilities through the resident bridge, handed to it as its private resource. Independently installed plugins provide a TypeScript library and optionally a private native executable. No provider lives in ModalAnyware. Project locations are agreed in plugin-packages-k6.
' Build: plantuml -tsvg packages.puml

skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam defaultFontColor #25364B
skinparam titleFontSize 22
skinparam captionFontSize 16
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #526B86
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #E8F0F8
  BorderColor #98ADC3
  FontColor #25364B
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #EEF4FA
  BorderColor #98ADC3
  FontColor #25364B
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8C7D7
skinparam NoteFontColor #33475E
skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #F1F5F9
  BorderColor #B8C7D7
  FontColor #33475E
  FontSize 16
}
top to bottom direction

title Package boundaries and application composition

component "User configuration\nComplete HTML / CSS / TS UI" as Config
component "ModalAnyware app\nSwift · a client of the Machine server" as App

component "UI facilities\nWindow host + shipped UI runtime and building blocks" as UI
component "Native key handling\nTap thread + delivery machine + interaction registry" as Keys
component "Plugin management\nFramework embedding + evaluator + resident bridge\n+ Machine client (server transport, capability) + tsconfig fragment" as Management

package "Plugin framework · PluginHost\nIts own project (AGREED)\n\nSwift side: catalog · resolver · supervisor · transport · evaluator protocol\nScript side: lowering · loader · plugin-host · connections" as Framework
package "Machine server\nIts own project and application (AGREED)\n\nMachine package: engine · Provider contract · Reference · Snapshot · MachineError\nTransport + capability model (its design) · LLM skill set\nProviders as its plugins: desktop provider first" as Machine

package "First-party plugin · modalanyware\nBundled plugin package (AGREED)" as FirstParty {
  component "Public TS API\nDefinitions · commands · machine facade · template helpers" as Facade
}

package "Independently installed plugin" as Plugin {
  component "Public TS library\nexports = API" as Library
  component "Optional private executable\nSwift / Rust / other" as Native
}

Config ..> Facade : imports
Config ..> Library : imports by id
Facade ..> Management : resident bridge\n(its private resource)
App *-- UI
App *-- Keys
App *-- Management
Management ..> Machine : client over the\nserver's transport
Management ..> Framework : embeds; implements\nthe evaluator
Machine ..> Framework : embeds for its\nprovider plugins
Framework ..> Facade : loads first
Framework ..> Library : loads on import;\ninjects connection
Library ..> Native : private JSON-RPC\nvia the connection

legend bottom
  <b>Notation</b>
  ◆—  Composition: app-owned responsibilities, each with narrow modules
  Dashed arrow →  Dependency: uses an interface or contract
  Folder  Package boundary; no process/deployment boundary implied
endlegend

caption AGREED (plugin-packages-k6): three projects; the framework depends on nothing here, the server embeds the framework, ModalAnyware embeds the framework and is a client of the server from its first increment.\nNo provider lives in ModalAnyware. A pure TypeScript plugin omits the native executable; no native host SDK is required.

' This is a static package/composition/dependency view, not a runtime sequence.
' The three app responsibilities do not mandate three monolithic implementation modules.
' Configuration defines the entire UI and accesses app facilities through the first-party plugin.
' Physical capture and immediate pass/suppress remain local native main-app behavior.
' The first-party plugin's private interface is the in-process resident bridge (configuration-ui-k5), attached as its resource.
' Machine contains machinery and Swift provider contracts, never concrete providers.
' Providers are the Machine server's plugins; ModalAnyware's Machine client carries the bridge's query and execute to the server.
' The framework depends on nothing here; the server depends on the framework; nothing depends on ModalAnyware.
' The framework's script side is engine-neutral JavaScript the host installs through the evaluator.
' Each host embeds its own framework instance; no shared system service is implied.
' Native companion operations/schemas belong privately to that plugin's TS/native pair.
' JSON-RPC 2.0 / UTF-8 NDJSON private pipes remain the agreed companion transport.
' No direct configuration-to-native-services or configuration-to-executable path exists.
' Package names are working names; the partition is what is agreed.
@enduml
